   "title": "Resistive switching test circuit",
   "page": 6,
   "description": "Measures the switching times. A gate pulse drives the DUT gate through Rg; the drain is loaded by RL from the Vdd supply, and the source goes to ground. Vgs is watched at the gate, Vds at the drain. The switching rows use VGS = 10 V, VDS = 15 V, RL = 0.75 Ω, RGEN = 3 Ω. td(on) is the time from 10 % of the gate rise until Vds has fallen to 90 %; tr is Vds falling from 90 % to 10 %; ton is their sum. td(off) is the time from 90 % of the gate fall until Vds has risen to 10 %; tf is Vds rising from 10 % to 90 %; toff is their sum.",
